---
description: "Testing — colocated vitest *.test.ts with AAA pattern"
globs: "app/**/*.test.ts"
alwaysApply: false
---

# Testing

## Context

Tests live next to the code they cover as `*.test.ts` and use **vitest**
(`describe` / `it` / `expect`). Examples: `app/src/reducer.test.ts`,
`app/src/store.test.ts`, `app/src/lib/text.test.ts`. Run with
`cd app && npm test`. Lint is not configured in this sample.

## Rule

- Add or update a **colocated** `*.test.ts` next to the module under test
- Use vitest APIs only (`describe`, `it`, `expect`) — do not introduce Jest or
  other runners
- Structure cases with the **AAA** pattern: Arrange → Act → Assert
- Cover new reducer actions / creators with at least one happy-path test;
  prefer also checking immutability where state changes
- Keep existing tests green; do not delete or weaken them to make a change pass

## How to verify

1. New tests sit beside the source (e.g. `foo.ts` → `foo.test.ts`), not in a
   separate `__tests__` tree
2. `cd app && npm test` is green after the change
3. Each new test has a clear arrange/act/assert flow (setup → call → expect)
